---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const calendly = 'https://calendly.com/contact-advised-seo/30min?back=1';
const jsonLd = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      "headline": "SEO for afro & textured haircare brands",
      "description": "Your customers search their type 4 hair routine on Google. Marketplaces and resellers bank the sale. Reclaim your direct sales with AfriRank.",
      "inLanguage": "en",
      "image": "https://www.afrirank.fr/images/article-capillaire.jpg",
      "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Francis Ndimba", "url": "https://www.afrirank.fr/en/about/" },
      "publisher": { "@id": "https://www.afrirank.fr/#afrirank" },
      "mainEntityOfPage": "https://www.afrirank.fr/en/seo-afro-haircare/"
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.afrirank.fr/en/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "SEO for African & Black-owned brands", "item": "https://www.afrirank.fr/en/seo-african-heritage-brands/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Afro & textured haircare", "item": "https://www.afrirank.fr/en/seo-afro-haircare/" }
      ]
    }
  ]
});
---
<Base
  lang="en"
  title="SEO for afro & textured haircare | AfriRank"
  description="Your customers search their type 4 hair routine on Google. Marketplaces and resellers bank the sale. Reclaim your direct sales with AfriRank."
  frPath="/seo-cosmetique-soin-capillaire-afro/"
  enPath="/en/seo-afro-haircare/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}>

<section class="hero hero--page wrap">
  <div class="hero-top">
    <nav class="breadcrumb reveal" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/en/">Home</a><span class="sep">›</span>
      <a href="/en/seo-african-heritage-brands/">SEO for Black-owned brands</a><span class="sep">›</span>
      <span>Afro &amp; textured haircare</span>
    </nav>
    <span class="hero-eyebrow reveal"><img src="/images/icon-orange.png" alt="" /> Product vertical</span>
    <h1 class="reveal">SEO for afro &amp; textured haircare: <em>stop feeding the marketplaces</em>.</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub reveal">Your customer knows exactly what she wants: "castor oil for hair growth", "protein treatment 4B", "moisture routine for coily hair". She's one click from buying. And it's a reseller or a marketplace that catches that click — not you.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" style="padding-top:clamp(20px,3vw,40px)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <figure class="article-figure reveal">
      <img src="/images/article-capillaire.jpg" alt="Woman with natural type 4 hair — afro haircare world" loading="lazy" width="1280" height="560" />
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap article reveal">
    <p class="lead">You've spent years educating this market. Your content, your lives, your wash-day tutorials taught a whole community to name its needs. Today, the demand you built turns into sales for others. This isn't an awareness problem. It's a capture problem.</p>

    <h2>Why afro haircare is a distinct SEO case</h2>
    <p>Your world splits into dozens of micro-intents, and each one is a page that can rank. We're talking queries structured by:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Hair type:</strong> kinky, coily, curly, type 3A to 4C, low porosity / high porosity.</li>
      <li><strong>Need:</strong> moisture, hair growth, breakage, curl definition, scalp care, the natural-hair journey / transition.</li>
      <li><strong>Ingredient:</strong> shea butter, black castor oil, aloe vera, coconut oil, protein, fenugreek.</li>
      <li><strong>Use / format:</strong> leave-in, deep conditioner, co-wash, styling gel, edge control, the LOC / LCO method.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each combination ("protein treatment 4C low-poro", "castor oil growth routine") is a way in. Multiply that by your catalogue: a map of territory few brands actually work.</p>

    <h2>Who takes your sales while you create the demand</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Community and Black beauty marketplaces</strong> ranking for "[your hero product]", often above your own product page.</li>
      <li><strong>Generalist pure players</strong> that crush category queries with sheer content mass.</li>
      <li><strong>Reseller blogs</strong> publishing "top 10 oils for hair growth" and slotting in their affiliate links.</li>
      <li><strong>AI answers</strong> (ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI) recommending a type 4 hair routine without ever citing your brand.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The three territories to reclaim</h2>
    <h3>1. Your branded SERP</h3>
    <p>If a reseller ranks above your official product page, you're funding their growth with your reputation. This is the fastest win. <a href="/en/own-your-branded-serp/">How to own your branded SERP.</a></p>
    <h3>2. Your category and ingredient queries</h3>
    <p>"Products for dry type 4 hair", "castor oil for hair growth", "low-poo routine": these non-branded queries should lead to YOUR pages, not just the marketplaces.</p>
    <h3>3. Your presence in AI (GEO)</h3>
    <p>Afro haircare is an advice-driven world — exactly what AI loves to summarise. <a href="/en/ai-visibility-geo-black-brands/">Become citable by AI.</a></p>

    <h2>The pages that make (or break) your SEO</h2>
    <p><strong>Product pages.</strong> Too often just an ingredient list. They need to answer the full intent: for which hair type, which need, how to fit it into a routine, how long before you see a result.</p>
    <p><strong>Category pages.</strong> "Type 4 hair care", "hair oils", "growth products". Your most powerful SEO pages and often the most neglected: a title, a grid, zero content.</p>
    <p><strong>Advice content.</strong> Routines, comparisons, guides by hair type. This attracts the customer upstream AND feeds your visibility in AI.</p>

    <h2>What it actually costs you</h2>
    <p>The leak lives in the gap between the haircare demand your brand generates and the direct revenue you bank. Three compounding losses: <strong>margin</strong> (wholesale price instead of retail), <strong>the customer</strong> (no email, no repeat purchase — and haircare is effectively a subscription category), <strong>the brand</strong> (a third party that owns your SERP decides the price shown). As a market order of magnitude, the share of afro haircare traffic captured by third parties on non-branded queries is rarely marginal; the Diagnostic measures it for YOUR catalogue. Estimate it with the <a href="/en/lost-organic-revenue-calculator/">calculator</a>.</p>

    <blockquote><p>The what and the how-much, I show you. The how — which page to optimise, in what order — that's the work of the engagement.</p></blockquote>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal"><span class="kicker">Frequently asked questions</span><h2 class="sec-title">Your questions, my answers.</h2></div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">My customers already know my brand — do I need SEO? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Exactly because they know you. Your reputation creates the haircare demand; SEO decides who banks it. If your resellers dominate your queries, you're funding their growth with your reputation.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">Is afro haircare SEO really specific? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>The mechanics are standard, the terrain isn't: ultra-granular queries (hair type, ingredient, porosity), heavy competition from community marketplaces, and an advice-driven world that AI summarises constantly.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">Do I need to create blog content to rank? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Advice content helps, but it comes after the essentials: reclaiming your branded SERP and strengthening your category and product pages. The Diagnostic prioritises so you don't produce content that serves no purpose.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">How do I get recommended by ChatGPT for a type 4 hair routine? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>That's GEO: a structured presence, a brand clearly tied to its benefits, and citable content. The Diagnostic identifies whether you're cited today and where your blind spots are.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">How long before I see results? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Reclaiming your branded SERP is faster than winning "castor oil for hair growth". The Diagnostic puts the quick wins first.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="links-more reveal">
      <h2>Go further</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/en/seo-african-heritage-brands/">SEO strategy for African & Black-owned brands</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/recover-revenue-from-resellers/">Recover the revenue captured by your resellers</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/seo-makeup-black-skin/">Makeup for Black skin</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/ai-visibility-geo-black-brands/">AI visibility for Black-owned brands</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta-band reveal">
      <img src="/images/icon-cream.png" class="icon-watermark" alt="" />
      <h2>Where to start: the Diagnostic.</h2>
      <p>I quantify the revenue your resellers capture in your place across the haircare world, pinpoint your blind spots (product pages, categories, content, AI) and map the prioritised plan. €290 (~$310), credited toward your first month if you continue.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href={calendly} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn--orange">Book the Diagnostic
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </a>
        <a href="/en/seo-diagnostic/" class="btn btn--cream">Learn more</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
